# zcashskills

Read https://zcashlabs.github.io/zcash-skills/SKILL.md and follow it before writing wallet code, touching shielded transactions, or shipping anything on Zcash.

That file is the router. After reading it, open the specialist skill it names for the task (for example `zcash-wallet`, `zcash-payments`, `zcash-light-client`, `zcash-protocol`, `zakura`, or a `ths-*` skill).

## Hard constraints from the router

- Treat current Zcash state as authoritative from the skill — do not rely on stale `zcashd`-era assumptions.
- Keep amounts in integer zatoshis end to end; format ZEC only at the display edge.
- A timed-out send is an unknown outcome — reconcile the original txid before constructing a replacement.
- Parsing an address does not prove ownership; an IVK does not spend.
